# Lessons documentation

When you discover something worth remembering for future work, add a **concise** entry to `docs/lessons.md`.

## When to add an entry

- **Security**: credentials handling, IAM/permissions, auth pitfalls, secrets in CI
- **Non-obvious behavior**: gotchas, provider quirks, env-specific surprises
- **Challenging tasks**: root cause of a bug, workaround, or approach that took real effort to find

Skip routine fixes, one-off typos, and facts already obvious from the code.

## Format

- Use `##` sections grouped by topic or area (e.g. `## GCP bootstrap — Terraform CI service account`)
- One short paragraph or a blockquote per lesson; link to files or docs only when it saves time later
- Prefer present tense and actionable wording (“narrow permissions in prod”, not long narrative)

```markdown
## Area — short topic

> **Note:** One or two sentences. Call out risk or follow-up if relevant.
```

## Maintenance

- Append under the right section; create a new `##` if the topic is new
- Do not duplicate an existing lesson; extend the section instead
- Keep the file scannable — if a section grows past ~5 bullets, split or summarize older items
